AWS DevOps Engineer – Interview Questions (4–6 Years Experience)

If you’re preparing for an AWS DevOps Engineer role, these are the real questions interviewers ask 👇

🔹 AWS Architecture & Design
 How do you design a highly available and fault-tolerant system on AWS?
 When would you choose ALB vs NLB vs CLB?
 How do you implement multi-AZ and multi-region architectures?
 How do you design zero-downtime deployments on AWS?
 How do you handle disaster recovery in AWS?
CI/CD on AWS
 How do you design a CI/CD pipeline using AWS services?
 CodePipeline vs Jenkins — when would you choose each?
 How do you implement rollback strategies in AWS deployments?
 How do you manage secrets in CI/CD pipelines on AWS?
 How do you secure CI/CD pipelines in AWS?

🔹 Containers & Kubernetes (ECS/EKS)
 ECS vs EKS — when to use what?
 How do you deploy and scale containers on ECS?
 How do you troubleshoot pod failures in EKS?
 How do you handle EKS cluster upgrades?
 How do you secure container workloads on AWS?

🔹 Infrastructure as Code
 Terraform vs CloudFormation — pros & cons?
 How do you manage Terraform state remotely on AWS?
 How do you prevent infrastructure drift?
 How do you design reusable IaC modules?
 How do you handle secrets in IaC?

🔹 Monitoring, Logging & Reliability
 Which CloudWatch metrics are critical for production?
 How do you design effective alerts without noise?
 How do you centralize logs across AWS accounts?
 How do you reduce MTTR during AWS incidents?
 How do you implement SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs on AWS?

🔹 Security & Cost Optimization
 How do you implement IAM best practices?
 How do you secure S3, EC2, and RDS?
 How do you control and optimize AWS costs?
 How do you implement least privilege across services?
 How do you handle security incidents in AWS?

💡 AWS DevOps interviews test architecture thinking, automation, and ownership — not just service names.
